{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pulls/17","id":4883985508,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVBPaw88AAAABIxu0ZA","html_url":"https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pull/17","diff_url":"https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pull/17.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pull/17.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/issues/17","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pulls/17/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pulls/17/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/issues/17/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP/statuses/97a01dab95bc53a08b8c372e3c3b04e69a923d7d","number":17,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"R5R3 closeout: preview.4 asset reproducibility, host-refusal discrimination and residual rulings","user":{"login":"shw097","id":219498218,"node_id":"U_kgDODRVG6g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219498218?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097","html_url":"https://github.com/shw097","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this changes\n\nOne file, +15 lines: `docs/install/ASSET_READBACK_v0.1.1-preview.4.json` gains a `reproducibility` block.\n\nIt records a fact an external reviewer can re-derive: the plugin ZIP that release `v0.1.1-preview.4` serves\nis the **byte-exact deterministic output of the commit the release tuple already records** (`cc6c193`). Two\nindependent builds at that commit produce 68,357 B / `545e359a…`, identical to the served asset. The block\ncarries its own claim ceiling: this proves provenance and determinism of the served bytes, **not** host\nacceptance, and **not** that the release carries later commits.\n\nNo product source, schema, workflow or test is touched. The release's own identity suite\n(`tests/test_r5r3_install_route_identity.py`, 10 tests) passes against this tree.\n\n## Why it matters for the open questions\n\nThe private-host import of this release's plugin ZIP was refused server-side on 2026-10-14 with no error\ncode, and the cause is still unresolved. This change removes build nondeterminism from the candidate causes\nand pairs with an offline member-level comparison against the package a previous round installed\nsuccessfully: every member shared by the two packages is byte-identical; only two provenance metadata\nmembers differ. Manifest location and manifest fields are therefore excluded as causes, and the surviving\nhypothesis is account/platform side.\n\n## What is NOT claimed here\n\n- Not host acceptance. The import is still unproven and the cause still unresolved.\n- Not that the release carries later repairs: the served wheel's `requirements.py` predates them; the repairs\n  are on `main` only. Whether to cut a successor is an owner decision, not this PR's.\n- No release, tag, install, directory publication or production promotion was executed in this round.\n\n## Residuals handed over (details in the evidence return)\n\n1. `NEW_RELEASE` — successor carrying the later repairs; contingent on the import decision.\n2. `PRIVATE_HOST_INSTALL` — one consented import attempt of the served package, then (only if refused) the\n   previously accepted package, as the discriminating experiment.\n3. Canonical SoD finding (pre-existing, not caused by this round): `check_sod(PLAN, VERIFY_SECURITY)`\n   reports `SOD_VIOLATION` because both lane routes' top-level model is `gpt-6.1-sol`. Resolving it is a\n   canonical route change, i.e. an owner/WorkOrder act.\n\n## Evidence return\n\nSeparate evidence branch `r5r3-closeout-evidence-20261016` (directory\n`R5R3_PREVIEW4_CLOSEOUT_20261016/`), carrying the build reproduction receipt, the control-plane probe, the\nPLAN-lane decision and its serving evidence, the TT dispositions, the runbook and the owner decision request,\nindexed by digest in `PACK_INDEX.json`.\n\nRollback: a single revert of this PR's merge commit. Nothing immutable is touched.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-16T05:33:02Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T07:32:40Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"2aa8547854fbdded8fa95a792aab3869184279c4","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"shw097-team:docs/r5r3-asset-reproducibility-readback","ref":"docs/r5r3-asset-reproducibility-readback","repo":{"id":1410587331,"node_id":"R_kgDOVBPaww","name":"PIPD-LS-SP","full_name":"shw097-team/PIPD-LS-SP","owner":{"login":"shw097-team","id":261346351,"node_id":"O_kgDOD5PULw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/261346351?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team","html_url":"https://github.com/shw097-team","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shw097-team/subscriptions","organizations_url":"